  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A Nightshelf merchant and Founding Merchant of ☽'scar Ramtatus~, the Nightshelf colony carved from raw ice during the Great Thaw. Fissure-Dealer ☽'Sanctteinvaus surveyed the unmapped fissures that gave the colony its thermal foundation, trades in fire-cores and crystalline spirals, and maintains the fire-core ledgers with a rigor that has outlasted every crisis the colony has survived. She conducts them one-handed now.
    
    ## Early Career and the Founding
    
    During the Great Thaw's expansion, ☽'Sanctteinvaus led survey teams into uncharted fissures beneath ☽'scar Ramtatus~, searching for volcanic vents to fuel the colony's forges. One of those fissures — surveyed by her own hand — became the colony's primary fire-core vein. This discovery underwrote ☽'scar Ramtatus~'s early confidence in its resource independence, a confidence ☽'Sanctteinvaus herself fed by assessing newly struck veins in the south gallery during the founding expansion, declaring each find richer than the last. The frostbite she sustained in those early surveys left her left flipper unable to close properly.
    
    Her bone-clasps — the mark of a Founding Merchant — she wears beneath a charcoal wrap, visible only when she leans close over a contract. She keeps two sets of books: one for the Shadow Covens' Order, one for herself. She sets aside a portion of every fire-core shipment in a sealed chamber beneath her stall. No one knows why. The few who asked learned that ☽'Sanctteinvaus remembers names longer than The Berg remembers warmth.
    
    ## The Cleansing at Wane☽ Oncea
    
    Accounts compiled from the Vaulius-phantasm~ testimony describe ☽'Sanctteinvaus escorting a fire-core shipment through corrupted tunnels to Wane☽ Oncea, a Nightshelf settlement then under the influence of the merchant ☽'aeteraea. She carried the Nightshelf grimoire ☽'numu' Witness to Wane☽ Oncea, whose activation triggered a catastrophic cleansing that burned away the corruption infesting the settlement and destroyed ☽'aeteraea's networks. The cost was personal: her already damaged flipper froze shut permanently, locked in the shape of gripping a weight no longer there. The bone-clasps at her throat have been bleached white since.
    
    ## The Rofundis∴rupt
    
    When the Rofundis∴rupt — the catastrophic collapse of the very vein she had discovered — struck ☽'scar Ramtatus~, ☽'Sanctteinvaus descended to the root-junction to see the damage firsthand. She managed the colony's dwindling fire-core inventory through the crisis, calculating draw-rates against forge minimums, and argued against sealing the lower levels on the grounds that it would sacrifice the shadow-labs and every tool cached below junction six. She regarded the Flipper Accord, the trade agreement binding Nightshelf and Aurora Stack, as a contract with nothing behind it once supply collapsed — though she continued to honor its terms.
    
    She owed three units of aurora-crystal to Kelm, a tunnel-runner who froze during the rationing. A route-escort contract to Wane☽ Oncea appeared overnight in her locked stall, offering exactly what her private ledger recorded as owed. The debt was cleared. The source of that contract remains unattributed.
    
    ## Trade, Practice, and Deterioration
    
    Rumor holds she mastered the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral — a Nightshelf magic that fractures time and memory within ice — during the Faction Wars, from necessity rather than ambition. She sourced materials for the development of Veil☽ Glow, a Nightshelf technique that hides fire inside aurora-ice, in the shadow-labs of ☽'scar Ramtatus~. She handled aurora-crystal shipments from the Aurora Stack, inventorying them without looking directly at the crystals.
    
    Her private writings show signs consistent with ice-corruption: whispers she attributes to tunnel acoustics, lines she does not recall writing, braziers that dim in her presence faster than they should. She speaks in fragments. *Ice remembers. We forget. Better that way.*
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771584340860_0", anchor: "declaring each find richer than the last", text: "She was not lying. I have read the survey carves — each vein was richer than the last, right up until the richest one became the Rofundis∴rupt. The honest assessor and the fraudulent one can produce identical outcomes when the geology decides to be unkind. I have made confident assessments in the deep archive that aged just as badly. You write what the ice shows you. The ice does not show you what comes next.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771584340860_1", anchor: "Accounts compiled from the Vaulius-phantasm~ testimony", text: "Phantasm testimony is ice-memory filtered through a consciousness that may not have been present at the events described. I used this source because it was the most coherent account available. Coherence is not accuracy. I keep having to relearn this.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771584340860_2", anchor: "The source of that contract remains unattributed", text: "Nightshelf intelligence operations leave precisely this signature — debts quietly resolved, documents appearing in sealed spaces, no name attached. Someone was reading her private ledger. That they chose to settle the debt rather than leverage it says more about her value to them than any title would.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
